    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Dallas Public Adjuster serves Dallas, Dallas County, and surrounding North Texas communities. We do not run storefront offices; we come to the damaged property, inspect it, document the loss, and work the claim with your insurer from there. The sections below describe the cities we cover and the kinds of severe weather each has actually recorded, based on the NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Storm Events Database.</p>
<p>Want to see reported events near a specific address? Search any city or ZIP code with our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a>, or browse the <a href="/storm-history/">Dallas County storm history</a>.</p>

<h2>Dallas: our primary service area</h2>
<p>Most of our work happens inside Dallas city limits, and the NOAA record explains why. Dallas County has logged 841 hail reports, 250 of them golf ball size (1.75 inches) or larger, with April and May the peak months and a smaller bump each October. On October 20, 2019, an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=856409" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF3 tornado tracked across northwest and north Dallas</a> from SH-348 and Luna Rd. across I-35E and Harry Hines Blvd. On May 28, 2024, a <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1186842" target="_blank" rel="noopener">75 mph gust was measured at Dallas Love Field</a> during a widespread windstorm, and on April 25, 2026, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1326034" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail near Dallas Baptist University</a> blew out car windows.</p>
<p>Water is the other big risk. The <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1053557" target="_blank" rel="noopener">August 21–22, 2022 flash flood</a> brought upwards of 15 inches of rain to parts of Dallas, and creeks such as White Rock, Turtle, Five Mile, and Ten Mile can rise quickly. Winter Storm Uri in February 2021 added a wave of burst-pipe claims. Dallas housing ranges from brick-veneer homes with composition shingle roofs to older pier-and-beam houses in Lakewood, the M Streets, Lower Greenville, and Oak Cliff, plus flat and low-slope roofs on apartments and warehouses. Repairs inside the city go through the City of Dallas Development Services Department; see our <a href="/local-building-codes/">Dallas building codes guide</a>.</p>

<h2>Cities we serve</h2>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/highland-park/">Highland Park</a></h3>
<p>An independent town north of downtown Dallas, known for Tudor, Craftsman, and traditional homes under mature trees. On May 16, 2021, a <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=961151" target="_blank" rel="noopener">brief EF0 tornado</a> began at Williams Park and uprooted a large tree in Goar Park. Tree-impact and older-roof claims are common here.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/university-park/">University Park</a></h3>
<p>Home to Southern Methodist University and the other half of the Park Cities. The same May 16, 2021 storm produced an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=961160" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF1 tornado just to the north near Royal Ln.</a>, and on June 13, 2012, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=386433" target="_blank" rel="noopener">baseball-size hail broke skylights at nearby NorthPark Center</a>.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/richardson/">Richardson</a></h3>
<p>A city of mid-century ranch homes and office campuses that straddles the Dallas–Collin county line. A National Weather Service survey found the <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1186739" target="_blank" rel="noopener">May 28, 2024 winds reached up to 90 mph</a> in part of the city, and <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1142401" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hail up to 2.25 inches</a> fell on September 24, 2023.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/garland/">Garland</a></h3>
<p>One of the largest cities in Dallas County, on the east side. Garland sits in the path of some of the county's most severe events: the <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=606471" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF4 Garland/Rowlett tornado of December 26, 2015</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1186742" target="_blank" rel="noopener">winds up to 95 mph on May 28, 2024</a>, and 3.75-inch hail on February 25, 2000.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/irving/">Irving</a></h3>
<p>West of Dallas, including Las Colinas and the area around DFW Airport. On May 24, 2011, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=306259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">grapefruit-size hail up to 4.25 inches</a> broke windows across Irving. EF1 tornadoes touched down in the city in <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1087760" target="_blank" rel="noopener">March 2023</a> and <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1248200" target="_blank" rel="noopener">March 2025</a>.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/mesquite/">Mesquite</a></h3>
<p>An east Dallas County city along I-30 and I-635. During the August 2022 flood, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1053519" target="_blank" rel="noopener">more than 10 inches of rain fell in a few hours</a> and I-635 at Scyene Rd. was closed by high water. Earlier, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=10352171" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2.75-inch hail on March 25, 1995</a> broke windows and damaged homes and businesses.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/carrollton/">Carrollton</a></h3>
<p>A northwest Dallas County city that extends into Denton and Collin counties. Reports include <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=766971" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail near the President George Bush Turnpike and Old Denton Rd.</a> on June 6, 2018, and a <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1186866" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roof torn from a commercial building</a> at Keller Springs and Midway on May 28, 2024.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/grand-prairie/">Grand Prairie</a></h3>
<p>A city that spans Dallas, Tarrant, and Ellis counties, with a large base of warehouses and distribution buildings. On June 13, 2012, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=386507" target="_blank" rel="noopener">orange-size hail fell at Belt Line Rd. and Warrior Rd.</a>, and a March 16, 2023 <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1087759" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF1 tornado peeled roofing off a warehouse</a> in the northern part of the city.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/plano/">Plano</a></h3>
<p>Plano lies mostly in Collin County, just north of Dallas County, so most of its weather history falls outside the Dallas County record shown on this site. Storms that hit Richardson and north Dallas often continue into Plano; NOAA's Dallas County entries include a 2003 thunderstorm that <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=5363907" target="_blank" rel="noopener">blew down power lines on the south side of Plano</a>.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/rowlett/">Rowlett</a></h3>
<p>A lakeside city on Lake Ray Hubbard in Dallas and Rockwall counties. The EF4 tornado of December 26, 2015 tracked into Rowlett from Garland, and an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=856502" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF1 tornado on October 20, 2019</a> damaged trees and roofs from Larkin Ln. toward the President George Bush Turnpike. <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1326100" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Golf-ball-size hail</a> was reported near Rowlett on April 27, 2026.</p>

