<h2>Other Dallas County communities</h2>
<p>We also work throughout the rest of Dallas County, including <strong>Addison</strong>, <strong>Farmers Branch</strong>, <strong>Coppell</strong>, <strong>DeSoto</strong>, <strong>Cedar Hill</strong>, <strong>Duncanville</strong>, <strong>Lancaster</strong>, <strong>Sachse</strong>, <strong>Balch Springs</strong>, and <strong>Seagoville</strong>. These cities have their own share of severe weather in the NOAA record: the highest measured wind gust in the county, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=5556565" target="_blank" rel="noopener">115 mph at Addison Airport on June 14, 1996</a>; <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=766939" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail in Coppell</a> on June 6, 2018; <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1105878" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4-inch hail near Cedar Hill</a> on June 12, 2023; the April 25, 1994 F4 tornado in Lancaster; an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=606463" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF3 tornado through Glenn Heights and DeSoto</a> on December 26, 2015; and water rescues in Balch Springs during the August 2022 flood.</p>

<h2>What stays the same everywhere we work</h2>
<p>Wherever your property is, the process is the same: a Free Claim Review, a written contract with fees disclosed before any work begins, a thorough inspection, careful documentation, and steady communication with your insurer. Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement, and you may rescind the contract within 72 hours of signing.</p>
<p>The area shares a few insurance realities too. Dallas County is outside the TWIA area, so wind and hail coverage typically comes from your regular insurer. Many policies carry a separate wind/hail deductible, so check your declarations page. Standard policies generally exclude flood. And each suburban city has its own building inspection and permit office, so code and permit requirements can change when you cross a city limit.</p>
<p>We handle <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail</a>, <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">wind</a>, <a href="/services/tornado-damage-claims/">tornado</a>, <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof</a>, <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood</a>, <a href="/services/freeze-damage-claims/">freeze</a>, <a href="/services/fire-damage-claims/">fire</a>, and <a href="/services/water-damage-claims/">water damage</a> claims for both <a href="/services/residential-property-claims/">residential</a> and <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial</a> properties. Not sure whether we cover your area? Request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> or call [[phone]].</p>
